article:
Yes! there is joy in the morning light;
Joy in the rising sun;
Joy at the open door of night
After the day is done.
Joy in the floating clouds o'erhead;
Joy in the azure skies;
JOY when the autumn leaves of red
Bring US a glad surprise.
Joy in the early flowers of spring;
Joy in the birds sweet song;
Joy the returning echoes bring,
Cheerily borne along.
Joy in the fervid MONDAY glow
Is it a pleasant dream?
Joy in the very winds that blow;
Joy in the dancing Streami
Joy in the glades, the rocks, the rills;
Joy on the mountain side;
Joy on the plains and wooded hills;
Joy on the rushing tidei
If we have hope for joys above,
Happy our lives may be,
Shining with rays of peace and love
Over a stormy sea.
B. F. NJ. Sours. in United Presbyterian

